Relevant columns and potential usage  
"ORDER_ITEMS"."sale_price": revenue part of profit calculation  
"ORDER_ITEMS"."inventory_item_id": links each sold item to its exact cost in INVENTORY_ITEMS  
"ORDER_ITEMS"."product_id": joins to PRODUCTS to obtain the product name that will be reported  
"ORDER_ITEMS"."status": allows exclusion of rows that are ‘Cancelled’ or ‘Returned’  
"ORDER_ITEMS"."created_at": micro‑second epoch time‑stamp used to map every sale to a calendar month (2019‑01 through 2022‑08)  

"ORDERS"."order_id": joins to ORDER_ITEMS (extra safety‑check)  
"ORDERS"."status": second place to eliminate cancelled / returned orders  

"INVENTORY_ITEMS"."id": joins to ORDER_ITEMS.inventory_item_id  
"INVENTORY_ITEMS"."cost": unit cost to be subtracted from the sale_price when computing profit  

"PRODUCTS"."id": joins to ORDER_ITEMS.product_id  
"PRODUCTS"."name": the product name that must be shown in the final result  


Typical conditions that will be needed  
• "ORDER_ITEMS"."status" NOT ILIKE 'Cancelled' AND NOT ILIKE 'Returned'  
• "ORDERS"."status"  NOT ILIKE 'Cancelled' AND NOT ILIKE 'Returned'  
• DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("ORDER_ITEMS"."created_at"/1e6)) BETWEEN '2019‑01‑01' AND '2022‑08‑01'  


Ten exploratory / building‑block Snowflake SQL queries  
Each query is different, returns at most 20 rows and every identifier is double‑quoted.

```sql
--Query‐1: Take a first look at raw order items
SELECT * 
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐2: Which distinct statuses exist in ORDER_ITEMS?
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐3: Which distinct statuses exist in ORDERS?
SELECT DISTINCT "status"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐4: Preview of non‑cancelled / non‑returned order items (inner‑join ORDERS as an extra check)
SELECT oi."order_id",
       oi."status"          AS "oi_status",
       o."status"           AS "order_status",
       oi."sale_price"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"       o
       ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE  oi."status"   NOT ILIKE 'Cancelled'
  AND  oi."status"   NOT ILIKE 'Returned'
  AND  o."status"    NOT ILIKE 'Cancelled'
  AND  o."status"    NOT ILIKE 'Returned'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐5: Join ORDER_ITEMS to PRODUCTS to see human‑readable product names
SELECT oi."id"                AS "order_item_id",
       p."name",
       oi."sale_price",
       oi."status"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     p
       ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐6: Attach unit cost via INVENTORY_ITEMS
SELECT oi."id"                AS "order_item_id",
       oi."sale_price",
       ii."cost"              AS "unit_cost",
       (oi."sale_price" - ii."cost") AS "profit_per_unit"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"     oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS" ii
       ON ii."id" = oi."inventory_item_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐7: Compute monthly profit per product for one sample month (July‑2020)
SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1e6)) AS "sale_month",
       p."name",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")          AS "revenue",
       SUM(ii."cost")                AS "cost",
       SUM(oi."sale_price") - SUM(ii."cost") AS "profit"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"     oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS" ii
       ON ii."id" = oi."inventory_item_id"
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"        p
       ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE  oi."status" NOT ILIKE 'Cancelled'
  AND  oi."status" NOT ILIKE 'Returned'
  AND  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1e6)) = '2020‑07‑01'
GROUP  BY 1, 2
ORDER  BY "profit" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐8: For the same month, pick only the top‑3 most profitable products
SELECT *
FROM  (
        SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1e6))  AS "sale_month",
               p."name",
               SUM(oi."sale_price") - SUM(ii."cost")                      AS "profit",
               ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1e6))
                                   ORDER BY SUM(oi."sale_price") - SUM(ii."cost") DESC) AS "rn"
        FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"     oi
        JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS" ii
               ON ii."id" = oi."inventory_item_id"
        JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"        p
               ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
        WHERE  oi."status" NOT ILIKE 'Cancelled'
          AND  oi."status" NOT ILIKE 'Returned'
          AND  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1e6)) = '2020‑07‑01'
        GROUP BY 1, 2
      ) q
WHERE  q."rn" <= 3
ORDER  BY q."profit" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐9: Prepare the 2019‑01 to 2022‑08 window (distinct months of activity)
SELECT DISTINCT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("created_at"/1e6)) AS "month_bucket"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
WHERE  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("created_at"/1e6)) BETWEEN '2019‑01‑01' AND '2022‑08‑01'
ORDER  BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Query‐10: Final pattern – top‑3 most profitable products for every month 2019‑01 to 2022‑08
SELECT *
FROM  (
        SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1e6)) AS "sale_month",
               p."name"                                                   AS "product_name",
               SUM(oi."sale_price") - SUM(ii."cost")                      AS "profit",
               ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1e6))
                                   ORDER BY SUM(oi."sale_price") - SUM(ii."cost") DESC) AS "rn"
        FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"     oi
        JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."INVENTORY_ITEMS" ii
               ON ii."id" = oi."inventory_item_id"
        JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"        p
               ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
        WHERE  oi."status" NOT ILIKE 'Cancelled'
          AND  oi."status" NOT ILIKE 'Returned'
          AND  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at"/1e6))
               BETWEEN '2019‑01‑01' AND '2022‑08‑01'
        GROUP BY 1, 2
      ) ranked
WHERE  ranked."rn" <= 3
ORDER  BY ranked."sale_month",
          ranked."profit" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progress from simple inspection to the fully‑shaped query that produces the exact data set requested (top three most profitable products per month between January‑2019 and August‑2022, excluding cancelled or returned items).
